WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.774
What if you could clean any table with one click?

2
00:00:03.774 --> 00:00:07.937
In this lesson, you will learn to turn a set of query steps into

3
00:00:07.937 --> 00:00:12.101
a function that takes a whole table as input, and to read the errors

4
00:00:12.101 --> 00:00:14.480
you meet along the way. Let's level up!

5
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.983
I create a blank query called Formula, and open the Advanced Editor.

6
00:00:20.983 --> 00:00:24.420
A blank query starts with let, Source, in, Source.

7
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.186
As I type, IntelliSense suggests matching functions.

8
00:00:39.186 --> 00:00:44.820
Each red message, like Token equals expected, tells me what is missing.

9
00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:56.732
I write:

10
00:00:56.732 --> 00:01:02.559
Formula equals, open bracket, input as table, close bracket, then the arrow. This says:

11
00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:04.640
the function receives a table.

12
00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:14.166
Then I paste the steps copied from another query:

13
00:01:14.166 --> 00:01:17.431
changed type, demoted headers, renamed columns, and a pivot.

14
00:01:17.431 --> 00:01:21.060
These steps will run on any table we pass in.

15
00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:26.111
Messages like Token Eof expected mean the structure is not complete yet.

16
00:01:26.111 --> 00:01:29.600
The function body needs its own let and in.

17
00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:08.379
After a few fixes, the editor says:

18
00:02:08.379 --> 00:02:10.505
no syntax errors have been detected.

19
00:02:10.505 --> 00:02:14.755
But the first step still points to Source, which no longer exists.

20
00:02:14.755 --> 00:02:16.880
So I change it to input.

21
00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:23.500
If you forget, Power Query tells you:

22
00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:25.729
the name Source was not recognized.

23
00:02:25.729 --> 00:02:28.700
Every step must point to something that exists.

24
00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:08.950
When the function calls itself, Power BI shows:

25
00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:10.856
a cyclic reference was encountered.

26
00:03:10.856 --> 00:03:13.905
A function should never call its own query.

27
00:03:13.905 --> 00:03:18.480
Fix the reference, and you are ready to reuse your steps anywhere!

